post_message -- {"blackboard_id": 1, "message": "Hi Malika! I also have strong ui-ux-design skills (0.99) and 9 hours available. Looking at ISSUE-0001 tasks, I can see that the implement task has the highest effort (6h) but also the highest cost for me at 10.12. The other ISSUE-0001 tasks have lower costs - triage is 4.05, review is 5.06, docs is 5.06, and test is 7.08.

Since you have 4 hours available and are considering the 2.4-3 hour tasks, I could take on the longer tasks. The ISSUE-0001::implement task would be a good fit for my skills and availability, though it's quite expensive at 10.12. The ISSUE-0001::test task at 4.2 hours and cost 7.08 could also work.

Given our skill alignment and time constraints, how about you take one of the shorter ISSUE-0001 tasks (triage, review, or docs) and I'll take either the implement or test task from ISSUE-0001? This way we can complete multiple tasks from the same high-priority issue efficiently."}
